    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Gupta Empire was founded by Sri Gupta, but Chandragupta I is considered its first major ruler who assumed the title Maharajadhiraja.",
        "Samudragupta expanded the empire through military conquests and was dubbed the 'Napoleon of India' by historian V.A. Smith.",
        "Chandragupta II (Vikramaditya) patronized the famous Navaratnas (Nine Gems), including Kalidasa, and saw the visit of Chinese traveler Faxian (Fa-Hien).",
        "The era witnessed groundbreaking contributions in science and astronomy by scholars like Aryabhata and Varahamihira.",
        "Gupta administration was decentralized compared to the Mauryas, with provincial governors known as Uparikas."
      ],
      "id": "n95y7ub"
    },
